## Summary

I shipped a production-polished native Apple (SwiftUI) `TimeMachineBanner` shared surface at full parity with `components/feedback/TimeMachineBanner.tsx`, following the established 10-file per-surface architecture.

**Delivered** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/TimeMachineBanner.*`):
- **Adapter** (pure core): `{when}` title interpolation, RFC 3339 validate/parse/format (web `looksLikeIso`/`toISOString`), locale display formatter (web `formatDateTime`), yesterday-noon picker seed, VoiceOver label builder.
- **Model**: P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry, connection axis, pure projection, `@Observable @MainActor` state-holder (picker toggle/open, submit, return-to-live), P1/S10 strings facade.
- **Seams**: P1/S8 source protocol + `AsOfDateStore` (UserDefaults RFC 3339 + In-Memory), `.live()` factory.
- **View/Views/States/Previews**: phase switch, `TSAlertBanner(info)` + action row + inline `DatePicker` (← web `datetime-local`) + freshness chip; loading/empty/error chrome; 8 previews.
- **strings** (8 web keys + native leaf/a11y), **Tests** + **ModelTests**.

**Every state renders** (loading/empty/error/data + stale/offline), all strings via the i18n facade, accessibility on every interactive element, P1/S11 telemetry emitted.

**Verification** (log: `…/logs/p4-apple-shared-surfaces-0143-TimeMachineBanner.log`, ends `EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`):
- Surface-scoped **green**: swiftlint `0/9`, swiftformat `0/9`, placeholder `0`, Swift 6 strict-concurrency compile of the real core = 0 errors, **executed harness 64/64** against the real source, in-module compile of all 7 app-target files = **0 `TimeMachineBanner` errors**.
